2. NASA's documented landing hazard categories
NASA's Lunar Landing Considerations document identifies several important engineering factors:
Threat category	What needs to be monitored
Topography	Craters, rocks, slopes and boulders
Geotechnical	Soil strength, regolith and dust
Lighting	Shadows and visibility
Thermal	Surface and hardware temperatures
Navigation	Position, altitude and velocity
Propulsion	Engine thrust and exhaust effects
Plume interaction	Erosion and flying particles
Source: NASA – Lunar Landing Considerations.
