3. How NASA detects and avoids these threats
NASA has developed the SPLICE (Safe and Precise Landing – Integrated Capabilities Evolution) technology suite.
Hazard Detection Lidar - NASA Science
science.nasa.gov
Its key technologies include:
Technology	Purpose
Hazard Detection Lidar	Scans terrain and identifies rocks and slopes
Terrain Relative Navigation	Compares live camera images with existing lunar maps
Navigation Doppler Lidar	Measures velocity and altitude
Hazard Detection Software	Identifies unsafe landing areas
Descent and Landing Computer	Processes sensor data and selects a safe landing location
How it works:
The spacecraft approaches the lunar surface.
Cameras compare the observed terrain with stored lunar maps.
Lidar measures altitude and velocity.
A 3D terrain map is generated.
Hazard detection software identifies unsafe areas.
The lander can divert towards a safer landing location.
NASA describes this system in its official SPLICE documentation.
